From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:19:08 +0000
Subject: Remove tracking parameters from shared links

Links that leave the browser through the clipboard or the share sheet
lose known tracking parameters: the utm_ campaign tags, ad click
identifiers such as fbclid, gclid and msclkid, email campaign
identifiers, and the share identifiers that some sites add to their
own links (si on YouTube and Spotify, s and t on X). The other
parameters keep their order and encoding, the fragment is kept, and
the "?" is dropped only when nothing is left of the query. Text that
is not a single http or https URL is not changed. Links the user opens
are not changed.

The cleaning runs where share requests are built (ShareParams) and
where a URL is copied (Clipboard.copyUrlToClipboard), and at the copy
and share actions that write a URL directly: Copy link address in the
context menu, Copy link in the app menu, in history and in bookmarks,
copying or cutting the whole address bar, sharing several tabs from
the tab switcher, the custom tab share button, and sharing a download
that has no file. Copying selected page text is not changed.

A switch in Privacy and security, on by default, turns it off.

